#. type: Title ==
#: usecase.en.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use case"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: usecase.en.adoc:6
msgid "In this tutorial you are going to explore features available to users through ChecklistBank by creating a new Moth dataset.  You will use four existing Lepidoptera (moth and butterfly) datasets in ChecklistBank. The three-letter abbreviations GLI, ALU, PHR and GAR will be used through the rest of this tutorial to refer to the following datasets:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: usecase.en.adoc:8
msgid "GLI: https://www.checklistbank.org/dataset/55434/about[Global Lepidoptera Index] – the primary dataset used in the Catalogue of Life Checklist for most groups of moths and butterflies"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: usecase.en.adoc:10
msgid "ALU: https://www.checklistbank.org/dataset/2207/about[Catalogue of the Alucitoidea of the World] – the dataset used in the Catalogue of Life Checklist for the many-plume moths (superfamily Alucitoidea)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: usecase.en.adoc:12
msgid "PHR (id: PLZ31420) https://www.checklistbank.org/dataset/31420/about[A world catalogue of Phragmataecia (Lepidoptera: Cossidae)], with a new species from Kazakhstan and Kyrgyzstan – a dataset summarising the names currently accepted for a moth genus, extracted by Plazi from a paper in the journal Zootaxa"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: usecase.en.adoc:14
msgid "GAR (id: PLZ41041): https://www.checklistbank.org/dataset/41041/about[A review of the genus Gargela Walker in China, with descriptions of ten new species (Lepidoptera: Crambidae, Crambinae)] – a dataset summarising the names of Chinese species a moth genus, extracted by Plazi from a paper in the journal Zootaxa"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: usecase.en.adoc:16
msgid "You will use ChecklistBank tools to structure a new moth dataset based on GLI and then modify it in the following ways:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: usecase.en.adoc:18
msgid "Exclude the butterfly superfamily Papilionoidea, to create a “moth”-only dataset."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: usecase.en.adoc:19
msgid "Replace the Alucitoidea section in GLI with the version in ALU ."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: usecase.en.adoc:20
msgid "Replace the Phragmataecia section in GLI (in the family Cossidae) with the version in PHR."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: usecase.en.adoc:21
msgid "Merge new species from GAR with those already in the Gargela section in GLI."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: usecase.en.adoc:22
msgid "The tutorial will finally show how the resulting dataset can be exported."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: creatingaproject.en.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Creating a new project"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: creatingaproject.en.adoc:4
msgid "Go to Datasets on the menu on the left side of the ChecklistBank window, and then click on ‘+New Dataset’."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: creatingaproject.en.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "img/web/datasets_page.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: creatingaproject.en.adoc:8
msgid "Complete the form:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: creatingaproject.en.adoc:10
msgid "Set a meaningful and clear title. For this tutorial use: your name followed by \"Moths of the World\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: creatingaproject.en.adoc:11
msgid "Select \"project\" for the Dataset Origin and \"taxonomic\" for the Dataset Type."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: creatingaproject.en.adoc:12
msgid "Set a Creative Commons licence for the project: “cc by” is appropriate since none of the four source datasets of this tutorial have more restrictive licences. It is important to consider that the licences of the source datasets must be compatible, that is, if the base source has a less restrictive licence, it will not be possible to integrate information from a more restrictive source. The licence of the project can be changed at any time."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: creatingaproject.en.adoc:13
msgid "Click 'Save'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: creatingaproject.en.adoc:14
#, no-wrap
msgid "img/web/create_dataset.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: creatingaproject.en.adoc:18 checklistassembly.en.adoc:21
#, no-wrap
msgid "img/web/add_root2.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: metadata.en.adoc:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Metadata"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: metadata.en.adoc:6
msgid "Once created the project, ChecklistBank will display the overview metadata page. Click on 'Edit' at the top right of the left menu to add metadata. Fill in as much detail as possible, specially in the following fields taking into account the following best practices:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: metadata.en.adoc:8
msgid "Give the project your own unique Alias – this will make it easier to locate in later steps. Consider using camelCase and spaces; avoid ALL CAPS and underscores."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: metadata.en.adoc:9
msgid "Description: A brief summary of the content and scope of the dataset."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: metadata.en.adoc:10
msgid "Contact: Person who can answer questions regarding the content of the dataset."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: metadata.en.adoc:11
msgid "Creator: Creator of the dataset."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: metadata.en.adoc:12
msgid "Contributors: All those who contributed to the creation of the checklist."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: metadata.en.adoc:13
msgid "Version: to be updated every time updates are made."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: metadata.en.adoc:14
#, no-wrap
msgid "img/web/metadata.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: metadata.en.adoc:17
msgid "Then click 'Save' at the bottom of the page."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: metadata.en.adoc:19
msgid "Once the Project is created, its Alias will be visible in the menu bar at the left, under which are all the sub items of the project."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Checklist assembly"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:5
msgid "Building a new checklist consists of several steps and tools, which are described below:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.1 Add a root taxon"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:9
msgid "To start the checklist assembly the highest taxonomic level has to be established. Under the Alias of the project on the left menu select the Assembly subitem, click on the Add root button near the middle of the window."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "img/web/assembly_fisrt_view.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:13
msgid "Enter the name “Lepidoptera” and click on Parse name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:14
#, no-wrap
msgid "img/web/add_root.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:17
msgid "A form will appear, change the Rank to order. This will change the display to include the fields shown in the image. Complete these as follows:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:19
msgid "Name status: established"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:20
msgid "Authorship: Linnaeus, 1758"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:26
msgid "Then click on 'Submit'.  The project now includes a single taxon (the order Lepidoptera) with a yellow triangle indicating that at present no sectors have been added."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "img/web/assembly_with_root.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:29
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.2 Add and manage sectors"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:32
msgid "The building blocks for a ChecklistBank project are called Sectors, these can be created by adding an entire dataset or a specific taxonomic group within a dataset. You can create as many sectors as needed, this gives maximum flexibility to assemble the project. There are several methods to add sectors to the assembly:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:34
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Union*: add all the descendants of the subject taxon, and ignores the name of the subject itself\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:35
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Attach*: adds the subject taxon and all its descendants\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:36
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Merge*: enriches the existing assembly with additional information provided by the selected sector like, new names, synonyms, authorships, and references among others.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:38
msgid "There are also several editorial decisions that can be made over any taxon on the project:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:40
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Block*: Ignores the selected name and its children.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:41
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Ignore*: Only the selected name is ignored.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:42
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Review*: Marks  that the selected name has already been reviewed and does not require changes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:43
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.2.1 Union "
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:46
msgid "You will start by adding the base tree, GLI, as the first sector with the union method.  Make sure that the Add sectors option is selected at the top of the window."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:48
msgid "On the search box on the right side of the window, enter “GLI” or “Global Lepidoptera Index”. Alternatively, type “55434”, which is the dataset ID for GLI. Wait a couple of seconds for the drop down list of datasets to appear."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:49
#, no-wrap
msgid "img/web/add_GLI.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:52
msgid "The right side of the window will refresh with the hierarchy for GLI."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:53
#, no-wrap
msgid "img/web/view_GLI.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:56
msgid "Select Lepidoptera on the right and drag it across onto or immediately below Lepidoptera on the left. You will be asked to specify how the GLI Lepidoptera should be added as a project sector. Select 'Union'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:57
#, no-wrap
msgid "img/web/union_GLI.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:60
msgid "The left side of the window will refresh to show that Lepidoptera is now sourced from GLI and will list just the first five children of GLI as an indication of content. The coloured labels will allow GLI to be distinguished easily from other sectors as they are added."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:61
#, no-wrap
msgid "img/web/assembly_GLI_view.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:63
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.2.2 Block"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:67
msgid "Now you are going to add a decision to exclude some parts from GLI: the superfamily Papilionoidea, the superfamily Alucitoidea and the genus Phragmataecia.  Click on the 'Source' item in the menu at the left of the ChecklistBank window. This will open a Select option with a second blue cog. Click on the cog."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:68
#, no-wrap
msgid "img/web/block1.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:71
msgid "You only have one sector in your project (GLI). Select this from the pop up search window."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:72
#, no-wrap
msgid "img/web/block2.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:75
msgid "A new view of GLI will appear next to a blue cog. This shows us the active source dataset for workbench operations. As more sectors are added, clicking again on the cog will allow you to switch source dataset."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:77
msgid "The initial view shows the Issues known for the dataset. GLI is very large and still being actively curated, so there are many of these, but they can be ignored for this tutorial."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:78
#, no-wrap
msgid "img/web/view_issues.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:81
msgid "Select the 'Workbench´ subitem for the Source view of GLI. The workbench shows all of the taxa that will be included in your project dataset from GLI."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:82
#, no-wrap
msgid "img/web/block3.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:85
msgid "Type “Papilionoidea” in the Search box at the top of the window and hit Enter. The record for the butterfly superfamily Papilionoidea will be the only one shown. You can alternatively filter taxa using ranks or higher taxon or other options that can be selected by clicking on 'Advanced'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:86
#, no-wrap
msgid "img/web/block4.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:89
msgid "Select \"Block\" from the dropdown at the left above the taxon list (just below “Reset search”)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:90
#, no-wrap
msgid "img/web/block5.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:93
msgid "Select \"Papilionoidea\" from the list and click on 'Apply selected decision'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:94
#, no-wrap
msgid "img/web/block6.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:97
msgid "If you click now on ‘Reset search’ (the red button on the left) and the ‘With decision’ radio button on the right, you will see that you have now specified a single decision, that Papilionoidea should be blocked. The same information can also be seen if you click on the Decisions subitem under the project menu."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:98
#, no-wrap
msgid "img/web/block7.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:101
msgid "When you populate the dataset, this decision will be honoured."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:103
msgid "Repeat the same steps (Source: Global Lepidoptera Index > Workbench > search for taxon > Block taxon) for the superfamily Alucitoidea and the genus Phragmataecia."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:104
#, no-wrap
msgid "img/web/block8.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:106
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.2.3  Attach "
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:109
msgid "Unlike GLI, the dataset Catalogue of the Alucitoidea of the World (ALU) includes higher classification all the way up to the kingdom, thus you are going to replace GLI Alucitoidea sector with ALU source."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:111
msgid "In the project, select the Assembly subitem at the left and make sure the Add sectors view is selected (at the top of the window). Enter “Alucitoidea” in the search field on the right, wait a couple of seconds for the drop down list of datasets to appear, and select the first dataset (id:2207)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:112
#, no-wrap
msgid "img/web/attach1.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:115
msgid "Select the small arrows next to each name until the superfamily Alucitoidea appears. Alternatively, type “Alucitoidea” in the second search box on the right of the window and select it directly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:116
#, no-wrap
msgid "img/web/attach2.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:119
msgid "Drag Alucitoidea from ALU on the right onto Lepidoptera in your project on the left. Select Attach to include it as a child taxon."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:120
#, no-wrap
msgid "img/web/attach3.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:123
msgid "The project display will now show that you have added two sectors. Note also the blue eye symbol and source link at the top right. This is a quick way to select the current dataset as the current source dataset in the Source submenu."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:124
#, no-wrap
msgid "img/web/attach4.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:127
msgid "At this point the tool only shows an overview of the higher classification, to continue creating sectors at a more specific level it is best to synchronize all sectors so the entire assembly can be explored and managed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:129
msgid "Select the Sectors item in the menu at the left below the alias of your project. This view allows you to synchronise the content from each sector into your project."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:131
msgid "Select the 'Sync all sectors' button and click 'Yes'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:132
#, no-wrap
msgid "img/web/sync1.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:135
msgid "Return to the Assembly subitem. You will see the view of the project contents beginning to be updated. This will take several minutes, grab a cup of coffee and wait for it to complete. You can Refresh the display to see progress."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:136
#, no-wrap
msgid "img/web/sync2.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:139
msgid "Alternatively, you may click on the double arrowed circle on the top right and see the Sync state."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:141
#, no-wrap
msgid "img/web/sync3.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:144
msgid "Now let's Attach a new sector."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:146
msgid "In the Assembly > Add sectors view, search on the left side for the tribe Zeuzerini and on the right search for Phragmataecia and select dataset PLZ31420 (PHR)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:147 checklistassembly.en.adoc:152
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:157 checklistassembly.en.adoc:167
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:171 checklistassembly.en.adoc:175
#, no-wrap
msgid "img/web/CLB-search.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:150
msgid "Find the genus Phragmataecia from PHR and drag it onto Zeuzerini in the project. Select Attach to insert the genus as a new sector."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:156
msgid "A new sector (with a new colour) will appear on the left. The PHR (alias is PLZ31420). The sector has not yet been synchronised so it shows no child taxa."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:159
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.2.4 Merge"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:162
msgid "With this option to add sectors you can combine information from two or more sources. Here you will merge the species from GLI and those from the checklist derived from GAR, the paper “A review of the genus Gargela Walker in China…” (PLZ41041) that are not included in GLI."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:164
msgid "Go again to the Assembly > Add sectors view, search on the left side for the genus Gargela and on the right search for Gargela and select the dataset PLZ41041 (GAR)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:166
msgid "Drag the genus Gargela from GAR onto the genus Gargela in the project view. Select Merge. It adds all taxa from the source dataset to the project if there is not already an entry for them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:170
msgid "Go to the Sectors view and select Sync for the two new sectors (Phragmataecia and Gargela)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: checklistassembly.en.adoc:174
msgid "Following the synchronisation, the additional taxa will appear in the project view under Assembly, you can identify the merged taxa by a yellow square with the letter “m”."
msgstr ""

